cd sps
to obtain GNU compiler 9.3.0
. ./.eccc_setup_gnu
to obtain Intel compiler
. ./.eccc_setup_intel

Interactive:
sps.sh --dircfg configurations/SPS_cfgs --ptopo=2x2 --btopo=1x1 --inorder > list_sps 2>&1

Verify namelists (example):
checknml share/configurations/SPS_cfgs/cfg_0000/sps.cfg
checknml share/configurations/SPS_isba_cfgs/cfg_0000/sps.cfg

Interactive to run all test cases (Can do this on Science backend node):
---------------
sps_tests.sh

Batch to run all test cases
----------------
Put the following lines in a file called myjob.sh

!/bin/bash
cd [path of your SPS git clone]
. ./.eccc_setup_intel
cd $SPS_WORK
sps_tests.sh
#For Science: ord_soumet -jobfile myjob.sh -jn job_SPStests -d ppp5 -mpi -norerun -c 80x1 -m 2G -w 30 -v -listing $HOME/listings
#For GPSCC: ord_soumet -jobfile myjob.sh -jn job_SPStests -d gpscc3 -project eccc_pegasus_mrd -mpi -norerun -c 80x1 -m 2G -w 30 -v -listing $HOME/listings -qos low

Batch example to run 1 case for Intel
-----------------
in mySPS_cfgs.job

!/bin/bash
cd [path of your SPS git clone]
. ./.eccc_setup_intel
cd $SPS_WORK
sps.sh --dircfg configurations/SPS_cfgs --ptopo=2x2 --btopo=1x1 > list_sps_cfgs 2>&1

then submit mySPS_cfgs.job using ord_soumet (note: 2x2=4x1)
#For Science: ord_soumet -jobfile mySPS_cfgs.job -jn job_SPS_cfgs -d ppp5 -mpi -norerun -c 4x1 -m 2G -w 30 -v -listing $HOME/listings

-----------------------------
CPU and PE topologies for the following configurations as tested in sps_test.sh:
(all use --btopo=1x1)

tape1_grid: --ptopo=1x1x1
SPS_cfgs:   --ptopo=2x2x1
SPS_isba_cfgs: --ptopo=2x2x1 
hrdlps: --ptopo=4x20
yin15: --ptopo=4x10
yan15: --ptopo=4x10
caldas_hrdps_isba: --ptopo=6x1
TEB_national: --ptopo=8x10
CSLM_cfgs: --ptopo=8x10
